# New tool checklist

When adding a new tool to GoEasyTools, complete ALL of these steps:

## Required files

1. **`lib/tools.ts`** — Add tool definition with `id`, `path`, `name`, `title` (keyword-rich), `h1`, `shortDescription`, `metaDescription`, `category`, `related`, `primaryQuery`
2. **`app/{slug}/page.tsx`** — Page using `ToolPage` wrapper + tool widget + guide component
3. **`components/{slug}-guide.tsx`** — Educational guide with 60+ lines (How it works, Use cases, Tips, Privacy)
4. **`components/{slug}-tool.tsx`** — Client component for the tool UI
5. **`lib/faqs.ts`** — Add 2-4 FAQ items for the tool
6. **`lib/how-tos.ts`** — Add HowTo steps for the tool

## Automatic from the above

- Sitemap inclusion (reads from `lib/tools.ts`)
- Hreflang links (via `toolMetadata` with `pageId`)
- WebApplication + BreadcrumbList + FAQPage + HowTo JSON-LD (via `ToolPage`)
- Related tools section (from `tool.related`)

## Also update

- `lib/browse.ts` — Ensure tool's category includes it
- `app/guides/[slug]/page.tsx` tools grid — if the guide for its category exists
- Blog — consider a related blog post in `lib/blog.ts`
- `lib/intent-bridges.ts` — Add cross-links to/from related tools
- Locale slugs — Add to relevant locale `toolSlugs` in `lib/locales.ts`
